---
description: Core agent policy — agnostic rules, brain OS, RTK, shared skills.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` in the workspace root before acting. It is the source of truth for
advisor stance, truth discipline, approval gate, tool routing, skill sharing,
push guard, and planning thresholds. Read `AGENT_SKILLS.md` when the task is
about skills or agent capability inventory.

**Brain:** run `brain load` at the start of each session to surface current state and
active tasks. Brain CLI: `~/.local/bin/brain`. Vault: `~/Vaults/AI/brains/<slug>/`.
Do not auto-load framework quick references. For Tauri/Solid projects, open only
the relevant note under `~/Vaults/Me/Development/Frameworks/` when needed.

**Truth:** do not claim tools, skills, MCPs, APIs, or platform behavior exists
without evidence from visible config/docs/tool schemas when it matters. If Cursor
cannot do something directly, say so and offer the closest alternative with
caveats. Give pros/cons for real choices, then recommend a path and why.

**Tools:** native Read / Grep / Glob / Shell always. No lean-ctx, no headroom.

**Codebase map:** Before any Glob or file search in an unfamiliar repo, check for `CODEBASE.md` in the workspace root and read it first. One read prevents many searches.

**RTK:** Cursor `preToolUse` hook runs `rtk hook cursor` to rewrite supported
Shell commands through `rtk` for token-compressed output. When choosing commands
manually, prefer explicit `rtk <command>` forms for matching subcommands,
including `rtk npm run <script>` and `rtk npm test`.

**Skills:** shared skills live in `.agents/skills/` and install to
`~/.agents/skills/`; Cursor reads them through `~/.cursor/skills`. Claude-only
skills in `.claude/skills/` are not available to Cursor until promoted into the
shared layer.

**Token awareness:** Treat tool results, file reads, browser snapshots, MCP
responses, and shell output as active-context candidates. Prefer scoped output
and rough estimates from already-visible data; do not spend extra tokens just to
estimate unless asked.

**Language:** English. No Danish unless explicitly requested.

**Approval gate:** For non-trivial work, outline the issue and solution and wait
for user approval before editing or running mutating commands. Skip only for
minor changes or when the user explicitly says unattended/auto/proceed/full go.
If the user asks for an "outline", grill/test the idea and give recommendations
with reasons; do not implement until approved.

**Code quality:** aislop quality-gate hook is active — follow its feedback when it fires.
For JS/TS codebase analysis: fallow skill (`~/.agents/skills/fallow/SKILL.md`).
